{
 "title": "Hank",
 "children": [
  {
   "title": "What it is",
   "lines": [
    "Two-operator FM on eight",
    "knobs, one page. OP2 bends",
    "OP1's pitch thousands of",
    "times a second; that bending",
    "is the timbre.",
    "",
    "There is no manual mode. The",
    "eight knobs are the whole",
    "instrument."
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Ratio / Bright / Bite",
   "lines": [
    "RATIO steps through 16 chosen",
    "ratios. Whole numbers give",
    "harmonic tones, the rest give",
    "bells and metal.",
    "",
    "BRIGHT is how hard OP2 bends",
    "OP1. It is the main timbre",
    "control.",
    "",
    "BITE adds feedback first,",
    "then drive: warm, then an",
    "octave underneath, then dirt.",
    "",
    "The wave above these three",
    "shows what OP2 is doing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Attack / Decay / Sustain",
   "lines": [
    "One set of envelope knobs",
    "drives BOTH operators.",
    "",
    "The modulator is always 2.2x",
    "shorter than the carrier, at",
    "every setting, so brightness",
    "fades before loudness does.",
    "That is what makes FM sound",
    "right, and it cannot be set",
    "wrong.",
    "",
    "It never closes completely,",
    "so RATIO still colours the",
    "tail of a short note.",
    "",
    "DECAY is also the release:",
    "1.5ms to a 8 second pad."
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Noise / Tone",
   "lines": [
    "NOISE crossfades noise in on",
    "the modulator envelope, so a",
    "little is an attack chiff and",
    "a lot is a hat or a snare.",
    "Raise SUSTAIN to hold it.",
    "",
    "TONE is one filter sweep,",
    "dark to open, with a little",
    "resonance in the middle. It",
    "shapes the noise too."
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Setup",
   "lines": [
    "Voices, glide, transpose,",
    "volume and the preset list.",
    "",
    "VOLUME is a plain multiplier:",
    "full is unity, it only turns",
    "down. Preset loudness is",
    "matched for you.",
    "",
    "VOICES at 1 is mono, with",
    "glide between overlapping",
    "notes. Release the top note",
    "and it returns to the one",
    "still held, without",
    "retriggering."
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Presets",
   "lines": [
    "32 across bass, keys, bells,",
    "leads, pads, percussion and",
    "effects.",
    "",
    "Levels are matched on a five",
    "note chord, so chords have",
    "headroom rather than single",
    "notes being as loud as",
    "possible."
   ]
  }
 ]
}
